1x1 controller 40 (self-contained firmware patch)

below is a self-contained firmware patch you can drop into your STM32/HAL project. It adds:
• an active probe mode (apply ±Δφ step/probe patterns and measure torque response),
• a simple adaptive mode switcher (2HB ↔ 3HB) that uses probe results and live telemetry (torque, temp, efficiency) to choose the best topology,
• UART command hooks to start/stop probes and control adaptive behavior,
• safe clamps, timeouts, and hysteresis to avoid oscillation / unsafe switching,
• logging/telemetry CSV format suggestions so you can collect probe data on the host.
I give full C sources (header + implementation) in STM32 HAL style and a short README block with UART commands, parameters, and recommended tuning constants.

What this patch does (high-level)
    1. probe_mode: performs an active measurement by toggling a small phase offset ±Δφ around the current DE5 phase setpoint for N pulses of duration T ms, recording measured torque (or torque proxy from ADC) for each step. From those samples we compute a simple SNR / gradient score that tells us if the change improved torque (i.e., probe detected constructive vs destructive phase region).
    2. adaptive_switcher: periodically (or after probe) evaluates scores across supported modes (2HB, 3HB). If one mode shows a robust advantage (score margin > threshold for M consecutive checks) the firmware will switch modes. Switching respects a cool-down/hysteresis period and safety checks (max switching rate).
    3. Exposes PROBE, ADAPT, SETMODE, REPORT UART commands for host control; telemetry CSV lines are streamed during/after each probe.
    4. All code uses simple blocking timing for clarity but includes notes on converting to timer/ISR-driven model.

